# No AI slop on the public site

Published copy (`*.html`, speech JSON, widget intro text, news notes) is for residents. Maintainer taxonomy stays in `.cursor/rules/`, catalog JSON fields, and git comments.

Before shipping any new or edited sentence, read it as a stranger. If it explains how this repo is organized, how a table is wired, or why a Case_ID was skipped, **delete it**. Finish every sentence. Do not paste assistant notes into the page.

## Internallish voice (ban)

Do not tell readers about JSON indexes, skinny rows, lookup jumps, flagship writeups, “catalog rows,” or “not a Case_ID.”

| Ban | Why | Public instead |
|---|---|---|
| “Adult names stay in the story writeups; they are not in the JSON index. Writeups that cite a wrongful ID jump from the table.” | Repo mechanics | “Search by city, technology, or ID.” |
| “City names with a local writeup jump to that panel… Month is the latest dated month in that catalog year when the dossier names one.” | Widget internals | Count + what the columns mean, then stop |
| “This is a catalogued Tennessee non-renewal in the municipal-cancellations index… are separate rows.” | Catalog taxonomy | The facts (cameras stay until January; sheriff use is off) |
| “Vendor PR, not a Case_ID.” / “Keep, not a cancel.” / “This is a keep, not a municipal exit, so it has no…” | Maintainer triage | “Cameras stay.” / “Holt voted no.” |
| “Six flagship writeups stay in full because council speeches cite them.” | Editorial process | Omit, or point to the tables |

Useful public status is fine: cameras stay, sheriff refused, council has not voted, Henry County IL is not Henry County VA. Cite `CAN-` / `FLK-` / wrongful IDs as footnotes, not as a lecture on why a row exists.

## Cut-off sentences (ban)

Do not ship a new clause that dies mid-thought. No `so it has no…`. No ending a **new** card on a dangling verb or preposition (`logging untrue reasons…`, `the Atlanta…`, `and…`).

If a one-liner must stay short, write a **complete** short sentence. Ellipsis is for quoted omissions in a source, not for the model running out of room.

## AI-tell (ban)

No First:/Second:/Separately scaffolds, em-dash piles, waxed eloquence, or “It’s important to note.” Write like a resident briefing neighbors.

## Check

Scan the **diff** before finishing. If any added line would only make sense to the person maintaining the catalogs, strip it in the same task.
